--
--   Description
----------------------
-- This test checks the handling of invalid code sequences by the PCS rx state 
-- machine. It exercises branches of the state machine which have not yet been
-- tried in other tests (identified by code coverage results).
-- NOTE : PCS mode will not run at 32-bit DMA mode because of 
--        bandwidth limitations. Test will be run at 64 bits instead.
--
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- * Checks that the PCS rx state machine conforms to ieee802.3 (2002) 
--   figures 36-7a and 36-7b.
-- * Tops up code coverage for the PCS rx state machine.
--
--
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 1Gbits/s, TBI, 64-bit DMA mode, with 
--    autonegotiation enabled.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
--
-- IDLE_CARRIER to RX_INVALID state transition
-- 4. With autonegotiation still enabled, send the following sequence to force 
--    the state machine from the WAIT_FOR_KD state into IDLE_CARRIER and then 
--    RX_INVALID states.
--       K28.5 (even)
--       D0.0  (odd)
--       K28.5 (even)
--       K27.7 (odd)  -- an odd aligned SOP
--    Visually check that this sequence is performed correctly on the waveform,
--    as there  is no method of automatically checking this (will also be 
--    checked by codecover results).
-- 5. Disable autonegotiation and allow synchronisation to occur.
-- 6. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received.
-- 7. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- FRAMES WITH NO DATA
-- 8. Receive a frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    The SOP group K27.7 should be successfully received in an even code group
--    whilst in IDLE_CARRIER state, but should then be followed immediately by
--    the end of packet sequence /T/R/R/ starting in an odd code group.
--    Ensure that the frame is not recognised.
-- 9. Receive a frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    The SOP group K27.7 should be successfully received in an even code group
--    whilst in IDLE_CARRIER state, but should then be followed immediately by 
--    the carrier extension sequence /R/R/R/ starting in an odd code group.
--    Ensure that the frame is not recognised.
--10. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received.
--11. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- FRAMES WITH CORRUPTED DATA
--11. Receive a frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    The SOP group K27.7 should be successfully received in an even code group
--    whilst in IDLE_CARRIER state, but should then be followed immediately by 
--    2 IDLE ordered sets starting in an odd code group. Follow this sequence
--    with enough frame data (including preamble & SFD) and carrier extension 
--    to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with a code error statistic.
--12. Receive a frame with configuration groups embedded within it.
--    The SOP group K27.7 should be successfully received in an even code group
--    whilst in IDLE_CARRIER state and followed by 15 data groups (pre/SFD/DA).
--    Then follow with a series of configuration group, starting on an even 
--    alignment. 
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped but with no statistic (undersized and 
--    code error). Read the link partner ability register to check that the 
--    configuration groups were successfully received (not possible as 
--    autonegotiation disabled)
--13. Receive a properly delimited 64 byte frame with carrier extension except 
--    that the /T/ EOP delimter is missing.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with both a code error and crc error
--    statistic.
--14. Receive a properly delimited 64 byte frame with carrier extension except 
--    that mid way through the data a /K/D/K/ sequence aligned at an odd group
--    is received.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with both a code error and crc error
--    statistic.
--15. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received.
--16. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- FRAMES WITH CORRUPTED CARRIER EXTENSION
--17. Receive a properly delimited 64 byte frame with carrier extension except
--    that only 2 bytes of carrier extension are indicated before a new SOP for
--    a second frame is received. (i.e. the end sequence is /T/R/R/S/ , with 
--    the /T/ even aligned.
--    Ensure that the first frame is dropped with an undersize statistic (no 
--    carrier extension) and the second frame is successfully received.
--18. Receive a properly delimited 64 byte frame with carrier extension except 
--    that the EOP sequence /T/R/R/ is immediatley followed by a data byte.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with a code error statistic.
--19. Receive a properly delimited 64 byte frame with carrier extension except 
--    that the last byte of carrier extension is corrupted with data in an odd
--    group.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with a code error statistic.
--20. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received.
--21. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- FRAME BURSTING IFG ERRORS
--22. Receive a burst of three frames, each of 64 bytes data and carrier
--    extended. The SOP (/S/) delimiter at the beginning of the 
--    second frame, shall start on an even code group. The SOP (/S/) delimiter
--    at the beginning of the third frame, shall start on an odd code group.
--    Ensure all three frames are received correctly.
--23. Receive a burst of four frames, each of 64 bytes data and carrier
--    extended. 
--  a)The byte before the SOP (/S/) delimiter at the beginning of the second
--    frame, shall be a /D/ even code group, implying that the /S/ is odd 
--    aligned. This causes a carrier extension error to be indicated in the
--    interframe gap, and hence is ignored.
--  b)The 2 bytes before the SOP (/S/) delimiter at the beginning of the third
--    frame, shall be a /D/D/ on a even code group, implying that the /S/ is 
--    even aligned. This causes a carrier extension error to be indicated in 
--    the interframe gap, and hence is ignored.
--  c)The last five bytes of the IFG and the SOP for the fourth frame, shall 
--    be replaced by the sequence /R/R/D/R/R/S/, even aligned so that the SOP
--    is odd aligned. Again a carrier extension error will be placed in the
--    IFG due to the /D/ group, but this will be ignored by the MAC RX module.
--  d)Ensure all four frames are received correctly.
--24. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- FRAME BURSTING SOP ERRORS
--25. Receive a burst of two frames, each of 64 bytes data and carrier extended.
--    The SOP group K27.7 of the second frame should be successfully received 
--    in an even code group, but should then be followed immediately by
--    the end of packet sequence /T/R/R/ starting in an odd code group.
--    Ensure that the first frame is received correctly, but the second frame 
--    is not recognised.
--26. Receive a burst of two frames, each of 64 bytes data and carrier extended.
--    The SOP group K27.7 of the second frame should be successfully received 
--    in an even code group, but should then be followed immediately by
--    the carrier extension sequence /R/R/R/ starting in an odd code group.
--    Ensure that the first frame is received correctly, but the second frame 
--    is not recognised.
--27. Receive a burst of two frames, each of 64 bytes data and carrier extended.
--    The SOP group K27.7 of the second frame should be successfully received 
--    in an even code group, but should then be followed immediately by
--    2 IDLE ordered sets starting in an odd code group. Follow this sequence
--    with enough frame data (including preamble & SFD) to satisfy slot time.
--    to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the first frame is received correctly, but the second frame 
--    is dropped with a code error statistic.
--28. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received.
--29. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- LINK FAIL WHILST RECEIVING
--28. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    replace the last 5 bytes of carrier extension with three odd aligned 
--    IDLE 2 code groups so that synchronisation is lost.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with a symbol error statistic.
--29. Receive a 64 byte frame with carrier extension to satisfy slot time.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received.
--30. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

